#: ../../source/setup/session_storage.rst:46
msgid "Your home folder"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/session_storage.rst:48
msgid ""
"Your home folder, ``/home/sepal-user``, is your permanent storage in "
"SEPAL. It is the same folder in every session, in the **Files** section "
"and in the apps you run, so files you save there are always available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/session_storage.rst:52
msgid "Use it for:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/session_storage.rst:54
msgid "code, scripts and notebooks;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/session_storage.rst:55
msgid "input data you use repeatedly;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/session_storage.rst:56
msgid "final results, exports and anything else you want to keep."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/session_storage.rst:58
msgid ""
"Because your home folder is network storage, each file operation takes "
"longer than on a local disk. This is not noticeable for large files, but "
"tasks that create or read thousands of small files — such as installing "
"Python or R packages, creating a virtual environment or unpacking an "
"archive — can be several times slower there than on the temporary disk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/session_storage.rst:64
msgid ""
"Your home folder counts toward your storage quota. You can see how much "
"you use in the **Usage** panel of the hourly cost button, :btn:`<fa-solid"
" fa-dollar-sign> x.xx/h`, in the lower-right corner, and in the **Storage"
" used** line of the **Terminal**. To find large folders, see "
":doc:`storage`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/session_storage.rst:70
msgid "The temporary disk"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/session_storage.rst:72
msgid ""
"Each session has its own temporary disk, mounted at ``/tmp``. The folders"
" ``/var/tmp`` and ``~/tmp`` (``/home/sepal-user/tmp``) point to the same "
"disk, so files written to any of them use the temporary disk and not your"
" home folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/session_storage.rst:76
msgid "The temporary disk:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/session_storage.rst:78
msgid "is **empty when the session starts**;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/session_storage.rst:79
msgid "is **deleted when the session stops**, whether you stop it or it expires;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/session_storage.rst:80
msgid "is only visible from the session that created it;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/session_storage.rst:81
msgid "does not count toward your storage quota."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/session_storage.rst:83
msgid "Use it for files you can recreate:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/session_storage.rst:85
msgid "Python virtual environments, Conda environments and package caches;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/session_storage.rst:86
msgid "intermediate rasters, tiles and other files produced while processing;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/session_storage.rst:87
msgid "downloaded archives before extracting the files you need;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/session_storage.rst:88
msgid "build folders and other temporary output of tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/session_storage.rst:92
msgid ""
"Everything in the temporary disk is lost when the session stops. Copy the"
" results you want to keep to your home folder before stopping the "
"session, and keep the files you need to recreate your environment (for "
"example, a ``requirements.txt`` file) in your home folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/session_storage.rst:98
msgid "Instance types with SSD"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/session_storage.rst:100
msgid "The size of the temporary disk depends on the instance type you start:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/session_storage.rst:102
msgid ""
"**Standard instance types** (for example, ``t1``, ``m2`` or ``c4``) get a"
" 100 GB temporary disk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/session_storage.rst:104
msgid ""
"**Instance types with SSD** (those ending in ``d``, such as ``m2d`` or "
"``c4d``, and the ``x`` and ``g`` types) use the SSD drives of the "
"instance as their temporary disk. Its size is shown in the **GB SSD** "
"column of the **Available instance types with SSD** table in the "
"**Terminal**, from 118 GB on the smallest types to 3,800 GB on the "
"largest ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/setup/session_storage.rst:110
msgid ""
"Choose an instance type with SSD when your temporary files do not fit in "
"100 GB, for example when processing large image stacks. These types cost "
"slightly more per hour than the standard type with the same CPU and RAM, "
"so a standard type is usually enough for smaller jobs. To compare "
"instance types, see :ref:`the Terminal section <terminal-instances>` of "
"the SEPAL interface presentation."
msgstr ""

